# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, not cosmetic.
#
# A fixture's committed plan is named for the sha256 of the *.tf beside it
# (scripts/auto_test/auto_test.py: fixture_sha). Before this file existed a
# contributor on Windows defaults (core.autocrlf=true) had CRLF in their working
# tree while git stored LF, so their fixture hashed to a different sha than the
# same fixture on every LF checkout: the plan cache hit locally and passed, then
# CI and the portal computed a different <sha>.json, found no plan, and reported
# `fixture-missing-plan` against every argument of the resource. Whole branches
# of finished work read as zero.
#
# fixture_sha now normalises CRLF and a UTF-8 BOM away before hashing, so the sha
# is checkout-independent on its own. This file is the other half: it stops the
# CRLF bytes entering the repository in the first place, which keeps diffs,
# rename detection and every other tool that reads these files honest.
#
# The default is deliberately global rather than a list of extensions. The
# failure it prevents is silent and expensive, and an extension list only
# protects the types someone remembered to add — the next fixture format, helper
# script or generated report added to the tree would arrive unprotected. `text=auto`
# leaves git's own binary detection in charge of what counts as text, so this is
# safe to apply tree-wide.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the types the harness or the linters hash or parse, so the
# guarantee is visible to anyone reading this file rather than implied by the
# line above. These are redundant with `* text=auto eol=lf` by design.
*.tf     text eol=lf
*.rego   text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.lock   text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary: never touched, never diffed as text. Stated explicitly so the
# outcome does not depend on content sniffing.
*.png    binary
*.PNG    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
